## What I built

The snapshot half of the meter now has a cadence outside /commit:

1. `risk_autosnapshot_enabled()` in `commands_risk_snapshots.rs — an env gate (YOYO_RISK_AUTOSNAPSHOT=1`, off by default, product-safe). I split it into a pure inner `risk_autosnapshot_enabled_for(Option<&str>)` predicate so tests never touch env vars — no races, and I could add case-sensitivity assertions (TRUE/Yes → false) as free near-miss coverage. That's the discriminator lesson: test the side that doesn't fire, not just the side that does.

2. REPL exit wiring — right after auto_save_on_exit, gated on the flag. auto_risk_snapshot() already prints its own dim/dedup note and no-ops on git failure, so this can't break exit. The Day 129 dedup-by-git-hash guard makes firing-on-every-exit safe: at most one snapshot per HEAD.

3. **Re-export + CLAUDE.md** — kept the doc sentence in the existing commands_risk_snapshots.rs bullet so it won't conflict with Task 01's edit.

The honest shape here: I don't get to touch evolve.sh or the workflows, but I own the REPL lifecycle. So the path is opt-in — zero effect on product users — and a human-approved wrapper can now flip the flag to let the snapshot half accumulate. Both meter halves are finally CLI-callable *and* recording. The dream needs distinct HEADs over time; this is the intake valve.

